Chapter: WhenArmTailCallTest

 Four recursion shapes, differing only in where the recursive call
 sits. Three of them worked on RISC-V for as long as anyone measured
 and the fourth did not, which is what made the defect hard to see: a
 tail call under `if` allocates no local, and a NON-tail call inside a
 `when` arm needs `ra` and therefore gets a frame anyway. Only a TAIL
 call inside a `when` arm landed in the gap, where the function was
 emitted frameless and its match then allocated a callee-saved
 register the frameless prologue never saved.

Section: Types

  Step =
   | Go (Integer)
   | Stop

Section: Helpers

  by-if : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  by-if (n) (acc) = if n <= 0 then acc else by-if (n - 1) (acc + 1)

  by-when-nontail : Step -> Integer
  by-when-nontail (s) =
    when s
     is Go (n) -> 1 + (if n <= 1 then 0 else by-when-nontail (Go (n - 1)))
     is Stop -> 0

  by-when-tail : Step, Integer -> Integer
  by-when-tail (s) (acc) =
    when s
     is Go (n) -> if n <= 0 then acc else by-when-tail (Go (n - 1)) (acc + 1)
     is Stop -> acc

  by-when-bare : Step, Integer -> Integer
  by-when-bare (s) (acc) =
    when s
     is Go (n) -> by-when-bare (if n <= 1 then Stop else Go (n - 1)) (acc + 1)
     is Stop -> acc

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "01 start"
    print-line-uni ("02 if-tail " & show (by-if 10 0))
    print-line-uni ("03 when-nontail " & show (by-when-nontail (Go 10)))
    print-line-uni ("04 when-tail " & show (by-when-tail (Go 10) 0))
    print-line-uni ("05 when-bare " & show (by-when-bare (Go 10) 0))
    print-line-uni "06 done"
  end
